
1. project creation
Python -m venv venv
./venv/Scripts/activate
pip install django django-pwa django-crispy-forms crispy-bootstrap5
pip install --upgrade pip
pip freeze

2. django application - (Django-5.2.18)
/venv/Scripts/activate  -start virtual environment
django-admin startproject mysite .
python manage.py startapp app
python manage.py migrate   - SQLite database is created


3. Creat admin user
python manage.py createsuperuser
python manage.py runserver localhost:9000   -- runserver

4. SQL cmd
enter password
show databases;
create database ft_pwa_db;

3. vscod terminal  - connect project to database
pip install mysqlclient
navigate to /mysite/settings.py add 'app' in INSTALLED_APPS, create new DATABASE , delete db.SQLite3
python manage.py makemigrations
python manage.py migrate
you can check database in mysql cmd - show databases; use databasename; show tables;

5. create new user since its new database
python manage.py createsuperuser
http:/localhost:9000/admin/login

6. configuring settings.py 
paste in settings.py STATIC_ROOT = Path.joinpath(BASE_DIR / 'static')
                    MEDIA_URL = 'media/'
                    MEDIA_ROOT = Path.joinpath(BASE_DIR / 'media')
create folder named media in base directory

7. configuring urls.py
from django.conf import settings
from django.conf.urls.static import static
if settings.DEBUG:
    urlpatterns += static(settings.MEDIA_URL, document_root=settings.MEDIA_ROOT)

8. in app folder models.py - make models
pip install pillow  
python manage.py makemigrations 
python manage.py migrate 
in app folder code admin.py
create forms.py in app directory
create urls.py in app directory
update urls.py in mysite  ---> from django.urls import path, include  urlpatterns = [
    path('admin/', admin.site.urls),
    path('', include('app.urls')),
]

frontend start
create templetes and static folder in app directory

path('', include('pwa.urls')),  ---> add in urls.py in mysite

